    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "BEFORE\nOmission fits\nConsumer(options?)\ntimeout?: number\nlimit?: number\ninterval?: number\nSeveral independent ways to supply thresholds",
      "id": "",
      "href": "#required",
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "AFTER\nPolicy must fit\nConsumer(policy, options?)\n{\nrequired section\nnamed fields · readonly numbers\n}\nRequired sections, or required scalar arguments",
      "id": "",
      "href": "#required",
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "See the actual contracts ↓",
      "id": "",
      "href": "#required",
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "01 / PRESENCE\nStated\nMake missing policy a type mismatch.\n\nOutput, resources, lifecycle, diagnostics and transport require their sections. Deeper readers and codecs gain required numeric parameters.\n\nReason: omitted composition must not recreate local defaults. ↘",
      "id": "",
      "href": "#required",
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "02 / OWNERSHIP\nStated\nRetire parallel tuning surfaces.\n\nRemove the CLI resource-policy factory, 26 constant declarations, eight workspace option fields and the executor’s output-options argument. Keep the existing package schema.\n\nReason: one policy owner; test tuning gets separate adapters. ↘",
      "id": "",
      "href": "#ownership",
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "03 / VOCABULARY\nStated\nName a purpose. Carry two budgets.\n\nAdd optional ordinary | status-observer purpose selection. Transport requires the existing delivery section with separate numeric reattachment and resume limits.\n\nReasons: distinct deadlines; a resume allowance per execution attempt. Loops are unseen. ↘",
      "id": "",
      "href": "#transport",
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "04 / SHAPE WIDTH\nUnexplained\nA section is still a structural shape.\n\nMost inputs ask for whole sections; idle lifetime asks for one field. Numbers have no unit, range or provenance brand. Slice width is not explained per consumer.\n\nThe types require names and primitive types; they do not establish snapshot origin. ↘",
      "id": "",
      "href": "#width",
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "05 / DIRECTION\nStated\nLess configuration can mean more assignable values.\n\nRequired arguments remove omissions. Holding dependency types fixed, removing required memoryCapBytes widens the workspace record shape. Resource shapes are replaced.\n\nSame stated consolidation decision; “removed” is not an assignability direction. ↘",
      "id": "",
      "href": "#directions",
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "06 / EXCEPTION\nUnexplained\nOne new capacity remains optional.\n\nStoredCommandOutput adds optional maximumRecordBytes, while its file decoder requires a number. Some formerly inferred inputs become explicitly annotated.\n\nNo reason found for that optionality; previous inferred types and defaults remain unseen. ↘",
      "id": "",
      "href": "#exceptions",
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "text": "07 / TEST BOUNDARY\nStated\nPut permissive construction in tests.\n\nSeven new helper files, plus local wrappers, offer optional legacy knobs and policy unions. Twenty-three test files change; their assertions are outside this view.\n\nReason: small test thresholds without production compatibility overloads. ↘",
      "id": "",
      "href": "#tests",
      "type": null
    },
    {
